-0.38,"prev_print":2.7},{"release":"2026-02-13","eve":"2026-02-12","ref_month":"2026-01","official":2.4,"tracker":2.56,"gap":0.16,"prev_print":2.7},{"release":"2026-03-11","eve":"2026-03-10","ref_month":"2026-02","official":2.4,"tracker":2.71,"gap":0.31,"prev_print":2.4},{"release":"2026-04-10","eve":"2026-04-09","ref_month":"2026-03","official":3.3,"tracker":3.66,"gap":0.36,"prev_print":2.4},{"release":"2026-05-12","eve":"2026-05-11","ref_month":"2026-04","official":3.8,"tracker":3.96,"gap":0.16,"prev_print":3.3},{"release":"2026-06-10","eve":"2026-06-09","ref_month":"2026-05","official":4.2,"tracker":3.98,"gap":-0.22,"prev_print":3.8},{"release":"2026-07-14","eve":"2026-07-13","ref_month":"2026-06","official":3.5,"tracker":3.61,"gap":0.11,"prev_print":4.2},{"release":"2026-08-12","eve":"2026-08-11","ref_month":"2026-07","official":3.4,"tracker":3.43,"gap":0.03,"prev_print":3.5},{"release":"2026-09-11","eve":"2026-09-10","ref_month":"2026-08","official":3.4,"tracker":3.54,"gap":0.14,"prev_print":3.4}],"n":12,"mae":0.174,"mean_gap":0.068,"sd_gap":0.208,"corr":0.931,"naive_mae":0.292,"note":"The CPI-Tracker variant rides the official rent and owners’ equivalent rent subindexes instead of market rents (under method v1.4, the rows before its move to v1.5, it carried both shelter weights on the official rent subindex), so on print eve it holds the prior print for the ~85% of the basket without a live source; its gap to the print is a plumbing check on the carry-forward, weights and YoY arithmetic, not a forecast."},"method":"Print eve: each variant's YoY on the calendar day before every CPI release since 2019-01 (reference month = the month before the release; the annual seasonal-factor revision that shares February with the January print is dropped), graded against the print as BLS quotes it — the NSA CPI-U 12-month change at one decimal — with the previous print as the naive benchmark; k=0 is that print (the month before the eve, the frozen standard), k=1 the print for the month the eve sits in, both with beats-naive counts and an autocorrelation-adjusted effective sample. Lead: the monthly average of each variant's daily YoY correlated with official CPI YoY k months later, k = 0–12, scored on the same months as two naive benchmarks — CPI's own persistence corr(CPI_t, CPI_t+k), and the real-time naive corr(CPI_t−1, CPI_t+k), the last print actually published when the gauge month closed; regressions of CPI(t+k) on the gauge, on CPI itself, and on both, with the joint t-statistic. Components: Pearson r on monthly YoY between each live input and the BLS subindex it feeds, the input shifted forward k months (rents 0–18, pump price 0–3, Manheim 0–6, farm gate 0–9); the naive columns are the subindex's correlation with its own value k months later and with its last published month. New-lease rent = chain-linked new-lease blend (Zillow ZORI 0.8 / Apartment List 0.2, renormalized over the sources present — the shelter model's own blend); all-tenant rent = tenure-weighted average of that blend with 4.5% monthly turnover over 48 months (the shelter model's own parameters). Latest vintage of every series; no smoothing, no window search, no parameter tuned to the result."}